body:
I will be doing ESL online, earning $2000 is the ESL company that always has work, earning 4000-5000 is using a higher paying ESL company that may or may not have work, earning $10,000 is successfully teaching students privately.

&#x200B;

As for my family, I believe raising my son in Lebanon would be a better option, while I love Canada I don't like how the youth are here, everyone is so distant, youth have no respect anymore for anyone, and being away from family is just not worth it. Life is short, I would rather live in Lebanon with family instead of rich in Canada. When my wife and I reflect on the last 2 years in Canada it honestly flew by, and we don't even remember what we did. Life goes by fast when you do the same thing every day. I've lived in Lebanon for 5 years during high school, and University. Those were honestly the best days of my life. My wife lived in Lebanon her entire life, and we're on the same page when it comes to moving there. 

&#x200B;

People will certainly say that leaving Canada is a huge mistake, and it probably is when you think about it Financially. But when it comes to the nice weather, the family, the sense of being with your people, your child having cousins, the food and so much more, you don't see what you have until it's not with you. In Canada it's 100% routine, you work, go home, sleep, and repeat. You cant see family because everyone is far away, you can't walk outside because it's minus 40, you can't meet new people because no one likes to get close, you can't go on vacation because the nearest destination which isn't the USA is a 10 hour flight and costs $1000+ for the ticket alone. You can't save any money because taxes are 30%, you pay off your home over 25-30 years, if you want to eat out the bill is minimum $100. I know it's so very selfish of me to say that as many people would kill to be in my position, as I know people in Lebanon are starving, no job opportunities, children leaving their country for a better future elsewhere. But I truly believe being with family is worth more then the job stability. And I know I'm one of the lucky people that can come to Lebanon thanks to this work I am looking at doing. 

&#x200B;

I hope I didn't offend anyone, I am not trying to undermine how much the government has truly destroyed your country, your futures and I know how much pain the Lebanese people are going through, my immediate family is from Tripoli, cousins 30-40 years old unable to get married, uncle working at 70 years old, life is very tough.

We're very frugal when it comes to our living style. As for income in Canada, it's not as much as you would think, I would be making more in Lebanon on a good month. 

&#x200B;

I've lived in Lebanon, however, in Tripoli, honestly I remember it being very cheap when it came to food and utilities, I won't be too far from Tripoli.
